WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Errata checks every draft against your approved brand rules.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:12.000
A creator writes a caption and sets its intent: goal, audience, call to action, channel and campaign.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:19.000
Six steps run. A flag survives only if it cites an approved rule or fact.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:24.000
CL-03: “assured returns” on a market-linked fund, quoting F-112 without its disclaimer.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:29.000
E-19: Oct 18 at Hall B belongs to another campaign. Caught without AI judgement.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:34.000
G-07: the brand is written PayWise, not “Paywise app”.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.000
WCAG 1.4.3: poster text at 2.89 : 1. Large text needs 3 : 1.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Fixes keep your intent. AI rewrites are re-checked before you see them.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:51.000
The claim goes to Legal, who signs off with a reason.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:55.000
The audit trail records who decided, when and why.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Humans approve. Errata never publishes.
